    <marc:datafield tag="520" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
      <marc:subfield code="a">Describes the natural phenomenon: &apos;lake overturn&apos; (limnic eruptions), where carbon-dioxide is triggered to erupt from previously carbon-dioxide saturated deep water lakes. The programme describes how such eruptions endanger the lives of wildlife, livestock and people surrouding such lakes through suffocation. A candidate for a future eruption is identified: Lake Kivu, on the border between the Democratic Republic of Congo and Rwanda, a lake that has over 2 million people living near its shores</marc:subfield>
